Native model viewer using raygui, raylib and TinyGL/VirGL.

    mk install
    modelview
    modelview /path/to/model.glb

Without a file it shows a generated torus. OBJ, IQM, glTF/GLB, M3D and VOX
use raylib's existing loaders. Materials use classic GL; programmable
shaders and physically based material effects are unavailable.

Drag to orbit, use the wheel to zoom, Space to rotate and R to reset.
The raygui controls open another file, show wireframe, toggle the grid and
lighting, and play embedded animations. Playback uses 60 keyframes per
second at speed 1. Raylib's animation API does not expose the original sample
rate; the speed slider can adjust models sampled at another rate. Static
views wait for input rather than redrawing continuously. Escape ends path
editing, or exits when not editing.

    modelview -n 120 -o /tmp/model.png /path/to/model.obj

This renders a bounded number of frames and saves a PNG. See modelview(1).
The viewer owns the loaded meshes, animation data and material textures;
replacing a model releases them. An unsuccessful open retains the old view.

New generated9 code under the root LICENSE. The libraries retain their
own licenses. No example assets are bundled with this program.
